hello — aarch64 sysl kernel entry (QEMU virt)
=============================================

Boot path for the QEMU virt board. Provides the platform-side
implementations of `arch_dispatch_sync`, `arch_dispatch_irq`, and
`arch_schedule_after_exc`, then drives two distinct demos depending
on whether the kernel-thread path or the EL0 path was selected.

Default (kernel-thread) demo: build two kernel-thread context
frames via `build_stack_frame`, kick off the first with
`arch_resume_process`, and let the generic timer's preemption
rotate between them. Each thread prints a tick + its id and
wfis until the next timer fires. Validates:
  - build_stack_frame
  - arch_resume_process
  - low64_irq save/restore
  - arch_schedule_after_exc swap

Legacy (EL0) demo: run a `b .` program at EL0 and let timer
preemption count ticks in hex. Kept under the `DEMO_EL0` val for
quick flip.

    module oskit.arch.aarch64.board.virt

    import oskit.arch.{page_alloc_zero, kernel_ptbr, vm_flush_tlb,
        vm_create_process_pt, vm_set_ptbr, read_sctlr_el1,
        read_esr_el1, abort,
        last_user_code_page, last_user_stack_page, drop_to_el0,
        sync_icache_line, vm_v2p, vm_copy_to, vm_copy_from,
        cntfrq_el0, cntp_tval_set, cntp_ctl_set,
        build_stack_frame, arch_resume_process,
        STACK_FRAME_SIZE, arch_cli, arch_sti}

    val DEMO_EL0 = false          // flip to true to run the EL0 demo

Render `v` as a 16-digit hex number (prefixed `0x`) to the UART.

    uart_puthex(v: u64)
        uart_puts("0x")
        var shift = 60
        while shift >= 0
            val d = int((v >> u64(shift)) & u64(0xF))
            if d < 10
                uart_putc(int('0') + d)
            else
                uart_putc(int('A') + d - 10)
            shift -= 4

GICv2 programming — QEMU virt wires the distributor at 0x08000000
and the per-CPU CPU interface at 0x08010000.

    val GICD_CTLR:       u64 = u64(0x08000000)
    val GICD_ISENABLER0: u64 = u64(0x08000100)
    val GICD_IPRIORITYR: u64 = u64(0x08000400)
    val GICC_CTLR:       u64 = u64(0x08010000)
    val GICC_PMR:        u64 = u64(0x08010004)
    val GICC_IAR:        u64 = u64(0x0801000C)
    val GICC_EOIR:       u64 = u64(0x08010010)
    val IRQ_TIMER: int = 30

    gic_init()
        var dctl: *i32 = *i32(GICD_CTLR)
        *dctl = i32(1)
        var isen: *i32 = *i32(GICD_ISENABLER0)
        *isen = i32(0x40000000)
        var prio: *byte = *byte(GICD_IPRIORITYR + u64(30))
        *prio = byte(0xA0)
        var pmr: *i32 = *i32(GICC_PMR)
        *pmr = i32(0xFF)
        var cctl: *i32 = *i32(GICC_CTLR)
        *cctl = i32(1)

    gic_ack() -> int
        var iarp: *i32 = *i32(GICC_IAR)
        int(*iarp) & 0x3FF

    gic_eoi(irq: int)
        var eoip: *i32 = *i32(GICC_EOIR)
        *eoip = i32(irq)

    timer_init_periodic(interval_ticks: u64)
        cntp_tval_set(interval_ticks)
        cntp_ctl_set(u64(1))

    var tick_count: int = 0

Kernel-thread demo state. Two kernel threads round-robin on timer
tick. Each thread has its own kernel stack (MAX_KT_STACKS slots of
4KB each, allocated in BSS), and its current saved SSP is kept in
`kt_ssp[]`. `current_thread` is the thread that was just running
when the IRQ fired.

    val MAX_KT = 2
    val KT_STACK_BYTES = 4096

    var kt_stacks: [2][4096]byte     // [MAX_KT][KT_STACK_BYTES]
    var kt_ssp: [2]i64               // saved SP_EL1 for each thread
    var kt_current: int = -1         // which thread is running, -1 = idle
    var kt_active: int = 0           // number of threads actually set up

Kernel thread 0: prints "A" on each scheduler pass and wfis.

    kthread_a()
        while true
            uart_puts("[kt A tick]\n")
            arch_wfi()

Kernel thread 1: prints "B" on each scheduler pass and wfis.

    kthread_b()
        while true
            uart_puts("[kt B tick]\n")
            arch_wfi()

    extern arch_wfi()

Initialize a new kernel thread: zero its stack, build an initial
EL1 frame with `entry` as ELR, and record the resulting SSP in
`kt_ssp[slot]`.

    kt_init(slot: int, entry: i64)
        var i = 0
        while i < KT_STACK_BYTES
            kt_stacks[slot][i] = 0
            i += 1
        val top = i64(&kt_stacks[slot][0]) + i64(KT_STACK_BYTES)
        kt_ssp[slot] = build_stack_frame(entry, top, top)

Sync dispatcher — the platform side of arch_dispatch_sync. Decodes
ESR and routes SVC to the syscall dispatcher. Anything else aborts.

    arch_dispatch_sync(esr: u64, frame: u64)
        val ec = int((esr >> u64(26)) & u64(0x3F))
        if ec == 0x15
            syscall_dispatch(frame)
        else
            uart_puts("[unhandled sync from EL0/EL1, ESR=")
            uart_puthex(esr)
            uart_puts("]\n")
            abort()

IRQ dispatcher — GIC ack, handle, EOI.

    arch_dispatch_irq(frame: u64)
        val irq = gic_ack()
        if irq == IRQ_TIMER
            tick_count += 1
            if DEMO_EL0
                uart_puts("[tick ")
                uart_puthex(u64(tick_count))
                uart_puts("]\n")
            cntp_tval_set(cntfrq_el0() / u64(5))
        gic_eoi(irq)

Scheduler — for the kernel-thread demo, rotate among the
registered threads. Save the current thread's SP_EL1 into
`kt_ssp[kt_current]`, pick the next one round-robin, and return
its stored SSP so the asm path resumes it. If no threads are
registered (EL0 demo), return the caller's SSP unchanged.

    arch_schedule_after_exc(ssp: i64) -> i64
        if kt_active <= 0
            return ssp
        if kt_current >= 0
            kt_ssp[kt_current] = ssp
        val next = (kt_current + 1) % kt_active
        kt_current = next
        kt_ssp[next]

Minimal SVC dispatcher for the EL0 demo.

    syscall_dispatch(frame: u64)
        var fp: *i64 = *i64(frame)
        val num = u64(fp[8])
        val a0 = u64(fp[0])
        if num == u64(1)
            uart_puts("[EL0 says ")
            uart_puthex(a0)
            uart_puts("]\n")
            fp[0] = i64(0)
        else if num == u64(93)
            uart_puts("[EL0 exited, code=")
            uart_puthex(a0)
            uart_puts("]\n")
            abort()
        else
            uart_puts("[unknown syscall num=")
            uart_puthex(num)
            uart_puts("]\n")
            fp[0] = i64(-1)

Entry point — boot.s calls this after mmu_init.

    kernel_main()
        uart_puts("SLIX aarch64 boot (sysl, MMU on)\n")
        uart_puts("Hello, aarch64!\n")

        uart_puts("kernel_ptbr=")
        uart_puthex(kernel_ptbr())
        uart_puts("\n")

        if DEMO_EL0
            kernel_main_el0()
        else
            kernel_main_kt()

Kernel-thread demo: build two kernel threads, arm the timer, and
kick off the first via arch_resume_process. The timer IRQ vectors
into low64_irq, which saves the frame, calls arch_dispatch_irq
(increments tick_count, reloads timer, EOIs), then calls
arch_schedule_after_exc which rotates to the other thread and
returns its SSP; arch_resume_process restores into that thread.

    kernel_main_kt()
        uart_puts("[kt] initialising two kernel threads\n")
        kt_init(0, i64(&kthread_a))
        kt_init(1, i64(&kthread_b))
        kt_active = 2

        gic_init()
        timer_init_periodic(cntfrq_el0() / u64(5))
        uart_puts("gic + timer initialised\n")

        // Pick thread 0 as the initial runner. Its frame's SPSR=EL1h
        // means arch_resume_process will ERET back to EL1, onto the
        // thread's own stack. Mask IRQs until we resume so we don't
        // race against our own timer before the resume lands.
        arch_cli()
        kt_current = 0
        uart_puts("[kt] resuming thread 0\n")
        arch_resume_process(kt_ssp[0])
        uart_puts("unexpected return from arch_resume_process\n")

Legacy EL0 demo — keep for regression testing.

    kernel_main_el0()
        uart_puts("sctlr_el1=")
        uart_puthex(read_sctlr_el1())
        uart_puts("\n")

        val p1 = page_alloc_zero()
        val p2 = page_alloc_zero()
        uart_puts("page_alloc_zero 1=")
        uart_puthex(p1)
        uart_puts(" 2=")
        uart_puthex(p2)
        uart_puts("\n")

        vm_flush_tlb()
        uart_puts("vm_flush_tlb ok\n")

        val new_pt = vm_create_process_pt()
        uart_puts("new_pt=")
        uart_puthex(new_pt)
        uart_puts("\n")

        val code_pa = last_user_code_page
        val stack_pa = last_user_stack_page
        uart_puts("user code_pa=")
        uart_puthex(code_pa)
        uart_puts(" stack_pa=")
        uart_puthex(stack_pa)
        uart_puts("\n")

        var code_word: *i32 = *i32(code_pa)
        code_word[0] = i32(0x14000000)
        sync_icache_line(i64(code_pa))

        vm_set_ptbr(new_pt)
        uart_puts("after vm_set_ptbr: still alive\n")

        gic_init()
        timer_init_periodic(cntfrq_el0() / u64(5))
        uart_puts("gic + timer initialised\n")

        uart_puts("dropping to EL0...\n")
        drop_to_el0(i64(0x60000000), i64(0x60002000))
        uart_puts("unexpected return from EL0 drop\n")
